WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.504
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.573
This is "The Tonight Show."

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.342
Well, guys,
I want to say congrats

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:12.378
to the Kansas City Chiefs
and Tampa Bay Buccaneers

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:16.616
on advancing to Super Bowl 55.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.484
That is right.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:22.122
Tom Brady is once again
returning to the Super Bowl.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.090
Man, between Tom Brady
and Joe Biden,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.594
what a month it's been
for 78-year-old white guys.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.598
Yep, Brady will be playing
in his 10th Super Bowl.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.065
How does he keep doing this?

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:36.102
I think he once got stuck making
small talk at a Super Bowl party

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.872
and vowed, "I will never put
myself in this position again."

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.140
It's like, "I'll just
play in all of them.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.042
If Brady keeps up this pace,
I'm just worried

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.011
where he's gonna put
the 11th Super Bowl ring

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.646
when he runs out of fingers.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.581
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.284
-Aw, no.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.419
-His toe, the big toe, maybe?

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:55.789
-Oh.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.290
-Meanwhile, the Chiefs are going

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.826
to their second Super Bowl
in a row,

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:02.128
led by star quarterback
Patrick Mahomes.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.064
He's 25, he's the reigning
Super Bowl MVP,

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.167
and he signed a deal
for $500 million.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.769
He might be
the only guy on earth

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.872
Tom Brady would
trade places with.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.907
Of course, it's not just
the quarterbacks facing off,

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.209
it's also the coaches.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.843
The Chiefs are led by Andy Reid.

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.945
The Buccaneers are led
by Bruce Arians.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.781
Can we see them both?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:25.985
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.187
Looks like
a before and before photo.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.589
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.426
Kind of strange that we've never
seen them at the same time.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.827
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.095
The only thing
we know for sure --

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.298
the winning coach will be
red, white, and round.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.032
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:45.070
Right now, the Kool-Aid man is
like, "I'm so torn. Oh, yeah!"

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.874
And this is cool, the Buccaneers
will be the first team ever

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.577
to play a Super Bowl
in their home stadium.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.912
Apparently, the Bucs saw the
entire world working from home

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.281
and thought, "Eh, why not us?"

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.351
One NBA team is allowing
a limited number of fans

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.319
back into their arena this week,

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.653
and they've come up
with a unique way

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:04.324
to keep people safe
from the virus. Listen to this.

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.759 line:0%
-The Miami Heat will use
specially-trained dogs

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.427 line:0%
to sniff fans for COVID.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.162 line:0%
If the dog sits, that signals

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.831 line:0%
they may have
detected the virus,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.267 line:0%
and fans will be asked to leave.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.168
-Yeah, these dogs
are super smart.

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:18.437
They can tell whether you have
coronavirus, drugs,

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.573
or a counterfeit ticket
from StubHub.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.274
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:25.244
That's right, the Miami Heat
will use COVID-sniffing dogs

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:28.814
to screen fans at games, which
brings us to our new segment,

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.916
"Uhh...I Have Some Questions."

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:35.321
-♪ Uhh...I Have Some Questions ♪

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:39.425 line:0%
-First up, since when are there
dogs that can "sniff" COVID?

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.894 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:45.832 line:0%
Next up, if a dog "sniffs"
COVID, won't it get COVID?

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.400 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.837 line:0%
Follow-up. Can dogs get COVID?

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.204 line:0%
If they can,

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.974 line:0%
and a common symptom of COVID
is loss of smell,

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:58.076 line:0%
how can you trust a dog
to properly smell more COVID?

00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:02.048 line:0%
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.483 line:0%
Also, are these the same dogs

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.051 line:0%
that sniff for bombs
at the airport,

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.753 line:0%
or are they completely
different dogs?

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:11.457 line:0%
If they're the same dogs, are
they getting paid overtime pay?

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.759 line:0%
I just have so many questions.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:17.563
-♪ I just have
so many questions ♪

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:20.065
-Speaking of dogs, yesterday,
President Biden's dogs,

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:23.235
Champ and Major,
moved into the White House.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.171
Yep, some dogs get to live
in the White House,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.540
while others have to
sniff for COVID.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.143
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.011
Not only are Biden's dogs
at the White House,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.947
they're sleeping
in the same dog house

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:36.249
that Dr. Fauci was in
all of last year.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.449
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:38.951
The dogs are actually
pretty busy.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.421
They're now in charge
of the Space Force.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.390
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.060
Meanwhile, Major hasn't even
been there a full day,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.561
and he's already passed
an executive order

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.730
that allows you
to lick yourself in public.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.799
Unbelievable.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.234
Some entertainment news.
Yesterday, HBO Max released

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.537
the first look of the new
"Godzilla vs. Kong" movie

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.839
that comes out in March.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.907
It looks insane.
Check out part of the trailer.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.310
♪♪

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.946
-♪ Yeah ♪

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.148
♪ Come on, oh, here we go ♪

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:13.253
♪ Give it a hundred,
never nothin' less, here we go ♪

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.787
-The only thing
more fun than that movie

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.856
is imagining two guys
in spandex suits

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.058
acting that out
in front of a green screen.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.694
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.369
Godzilla and King Kong fight
each other the whole movie,

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.637
but I'm told it's
the make-up sex near the end

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.106
that got them the R rating.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.309
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.644
[ Cymbal playing ]

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:39.912
This is going viral.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.615
A "Bridgerton" fan
spotted a modern-day mistake

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.516
in one of the opening scenes.

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.385
Take a look at this.

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:48.721
Can you guys tell what's wrong?

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.657
Here it is. Yeah.
The show is set in the 1800s,

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:56.562
but there's a yellow line that's
only used on modern roads.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.730
I don't know.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.064
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:00.633
I don't think
it's that big of a deal.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.302
-I do.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.770
It pulls me
out of the trance, man.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.505
If you want me
to watch your show,

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.874
then you can't be showing things
that people didn't use

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:10.743
or have in that era.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.611
[ Telephone rings ]

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.479
-Sorry, what is that?

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:17.049
Is someone's phone on?

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.517
-Yeah, sorry, man,
I got to take this.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:22.121
I've been on hold
for like an hour.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.656
Hello?

00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:27.093
Netflix?
-Oh, God. [ Laughs ]

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.862
-Yeah, cancel my subscription.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.396
You know why!

00:05:31.396 --> 00:05:34.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.869
-Oh. Alright.
Let's move on. Alright.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.475
Listen to this. An inventor
n Sweden has created something

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.578
to help keep
motorcycle riders safe.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.845
-Airbag jeans.

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:49.816
These pants have concealed
airbags inside the legs.

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:52.985
And if riders fall,
the airbags are triggered

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:56.355
and filled up
with compressed air.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.090
-Yeah, it's great
until you hit a small bump

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.059
and suddenly
turn into MC Hammer.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.827
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:04.596
And finally, a volcanic rock
was discovered in Brazil

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:06.565
that looks like Cookie Monster,

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:09.134
and it could be worth
more than $10,000.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:11.437
Check this out.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.473
Yeah.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.107
10 grand.
Right now, people are at home

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.508
with blue paint and a Sharpie

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:19.344
like, "Yeah, this rock also
looks like Cookie Monster."

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:23.148
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:26.018
Sorry, I'm just realizing how
different our monologue is now.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.420
Our last two stories were about

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.722
inflatable pants
and Cookie Monster.

